Package: cyclelanes
Title: Fetch and Classify Bicycle Infrastructure from OpenStreetMap and City Open Data
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
    person("Matthew", "Jorden", email = "matthew.jorden@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Pulls bicycle infrastructure for any place from OpenStreetMap via
    the Overpass API, normalises the dozen-odd OSM tagging conventions
    (cycleway=*, cycleway:left/right/both, highway=cycleway, bicycle_road,
    buffers, contraflow) into one tidy facility taxonomy with per-side
    classification, and returns an 'sf' object ready for mapping and network
    analysis. A pluggable registry of municipal open-data sources lets the same
    taxonomy be applied to a city's official bike-facility layer so the two can
    be summarised and compared. Ships with Denver, Colorado as the worked
    example.
